_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in : v4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee], v4.3, v4.2 \n\n### System information\n\nMacOS Sequoia 15.3.1 - Apple M2 - 8GB RAM - Forward+ (Vulkan and Metal)\n\n### Issue description\n\nMaking a window with a transparent background in MacOS gets all it's window decorations removed (like the titlebar and the border arround it)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/98414258-142d-43a5-a80e-11508b8b3211)\n\nLoading the same project without any settings changed in Fedora 41 with Wayland shows the correct behavior (showing window decoration)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bdcc6b23-1945-45c6-8a79-7ac481bb5b09)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create new project with a Node2D scene\n2. Go to project settings and set the following settings as `true` to make a true transparent window:\n> `display/window/size/transparent`\n> `display/window/per_pixel_transparency/allowed`\n>`rendering/viewport/transparent_background`\n3. Keep `display/window/size/borderless` disabled\n4. (optional) add a `ColorRect` with some transparency so we can see where the window is\n5. Run the project and look at the game window without any decoration\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[BlurApp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19097656/BlurApp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com